From: Stephen Trotter <33046718+sjtrotter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:07:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] RDP: test the protected connection-file helpers

Nothing in the tree exercised the code that reads and filters a protected
connection file, although it is the part of the RDP plugin that handles a
file from outside the profile store: bounds and ownership checks, two text
encodings, the ARM classification, and the allowlist that decides what
reaches FreeRDP's native parser.

Add a CTest target for those helpers. rdp_rdpw.c depends on GLib alone, so
the test links it directly and needs neither FreeRDP, a display, nor a
session; it covers the size bound and the file-type check, the refusal to
follow a symbolic link, UTF-8 and UTF-16 decoding of the same file, invalid
and NUL-bearing text, the three classifications, the keys the allowlist keeps
and drops, the refusal of a buffer holding an embedded "/" command-line
argument, and that a carriage return inside a line hides nothing from either
the allowlist or the classification.

Testing is opt-in: -DBUILD_TESTING=ON adds the target and enables ctest,
and a default build is unchanged. The fixture is a synthetic Azure Virtual
Desktop file whose hosts, tenant, and user are invented and which carries
no signature.

Build and run it with:

    cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
    cmake --build build --target test-rdp-rdpw
    ctest --test-dir build

Tested with FreeRDP 3.30.0. The series requires FreeRDP 3.16.0 or
newer: FreeRDP_GatewayAvdScope and FreeRDP_GatewayAvdAccessAadFormat
were added in that release, and every other API used is older.

This change was prepared with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) and was
reviewed and tested by the author.
